DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     fdt_pinctrl(4) provides an API for manipulating I/O pin configurations on
     pinmux controllers and pinmux clients.  On the controller side, the stan‐
     dard newbus probe and attach methods are implemented.  As part of han‐
     dling attach, it calls the ffddtt__ppiinnccttrrll__rreeggiisstteerr() function to register
     itself as a pinmux controller.  Then ffddtt__ppiinnccttrrll__ccoonnffiigguurree__ttrreeee() is used
     to walk the device tree and configure pins specified by the pinctrl-0
     property for all active devices.  The driver also implements the
     ffddtt__ppiinnccttrrll__ccoonnffiigguurree() method, which allows client devices to change
     their pin configurations after startup.  If a client device requires a
     pin configuration change at some point of its lifecycle, it uses the
     ffddtt__ppiinnccttrrll__ccoonnffiigguurree() or ffddtt__ppiinnccttrrll__ccoonnffiigguurree__bbyy__nnaammee() functions.

     ffddtt__ppiinnccttrrll__ccoonnffiigguurree() is used by client device _c_l_i_e_n_t to request a pin
     configuration described by the pinctrl-N property with index _i_n_d_e_x.

     ffddtt__ppiinnccttrrll__ccoonnffiigguurree__bbyy__nnaammee() is used by client device _c_l_i_e_n_t to re‐
     quest the pin configuration with name _n_a_m_e.

     ffddtt__ppiinnccttrrll__rreeggiisstteerr() registers a pinctrl driver so that it can be used
     by other devices which call ffddtt__ppiinnccttrrll__ccoonnffiigguurree() or
     ffddtt__ppiinnccttrrll__ccoonnffiigguurree__bbyy__nnaammee().  It also registers each child node of
     the pinctrl driver's node which contains a property with the name given
     in _p_i_n_p_r_o_p.  If _p_i_n_p_r_o_p is NULL, every descendant node is registered.  It
     is possible for the driver to register itself as a pinmux controller for
     more than one pin property type by calling ffddtt__ppiinnccttrrll__rreeggiisstteerr() multi‐
     ple types.

     ffddtt__ppiinnccttrrll__ccoonnffiigguurree__ttrreeee() walks through enabled devices in the device
     tree.  If the pinctrl-0 property contains references to child nodes of
     the specified pinctrl device, their pins are configured.

